urname>Sudhof</surname><given-names>T.C.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A tripartite protein complex with the potential to couple synaptic vesicle exocytosis to cell adhesion in brain</article-title><source>Cell</source><volume>18</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>773</fpage><lpage>782</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9753324</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CattaneoandPelicci1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cattaneo</surname><given-names>E.</given-names></name><name><surname>Pelicci</surname><given-names>P.G.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Emerging roles for SH2/PTB-containing Shc adaptor proteins in the developing mammalian brain</article-title><source>Trends Neurosci.</source><volume>21</volume><year>1998</year><fpage>476</fpage><lpage>481</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9829689</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Chouetal1987"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chou</surname><given-names>C.K.</given-names></name><name><surname>Dull</surname><given-names>T.J.</given-names></name><name><surname>Russell</surname><given-names>D.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Gherzi</surname><given-names>R.</given-names></name><name><surname>Lebwohl</surname><given-names>D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Ullrich</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name><name><surname>Rosen</surname><given-names>O.M.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Human insulin receptors mutated at the ATP-binding site lack protein tyrosine kinase activity and fail to mediate postreceptor effects of insulin</article-title><source>J. Biol. Chem.</source><volume>262</volume><year>1987</year><fpage>1842</fpage><lpage>1847</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">3100537</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Cohenetal1997"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cohen</surname><given-names>I.</giv